WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.910
Atoms are far too small to see,
let alone to count one by one.

2
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:09.230
Even a tiny speck of a solid
holds an enormous number of them.

3
00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:13.270
Yet a chemist can measure out
exactly six point zero two times

4
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.950
ten to the power twenty-three atoms,

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.950
using nothing more than
an ordinary balance.

6
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.210
So how can you count atoms
just by weighing them?

7
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.310
In this mission, you'll meet the mole,

8
00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.570
and the Avogadro constant.

9
00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:30.210
You'll link the mass of one mole
of a substance to its relative

10
00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:34.410
formula mass, and use that link
to turn a mass in grams into a

11
00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:35.950
number of moles.

12
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.500
Your mission: explain how
chemists count atoms by weighing.
